aved</name><conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic><conditions><leftValueReference>GetEarlierSavedForm.Id</leftValueReference><operator>IsNull</operator><rightValue><booleanValue>false</booleanValue></rightValue></conditions><connector><targetReference>AddSavedApplication</targetReference></connector><label>Saved</label></rules><rules><name>Abandoned</name><conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic><conditions><leftValueReference>forB_AbandonedDraft</leftValueReference><operator>EqualTo</operator><rightValue><booleanValue>true</booleanValue></rightValue></conditions><connector><targetReference>IsTheDiscardLimitReached</targetReference></connector><label>Abandoned</label></rules></decisions><decisions><name>IsTheDiscardLimitReached</name><description>Discards at most 3 abandoned drafts each time the form starts, so an applicant with many abandoned drafts does not hit the query limit. The rest go next time or in the nightly clean-up.</description><label>Is the Discard Limit Reached?</label><locationX>0</locationX><locationY>0</locationY><defaultConnector><targetReference>AddDiscardedDraft</targetReference></defaultConnector><defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel><rules><name>LimitReached</name><conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic><conditions><leftValueReference>varN_DiscardedDrafts</leftValueReference><operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator><rightValue><numberValue>3</numberValue></rightValue></conditions><connector><targetReference>LoopThroughEarlierDrafts</targetReference></connector><label>Yes</label></rules></decisions><decisions><name>IsThereASavedApplication</name><label>Is There a Saved Application?</label><locationX>0</locationX><locationY>0</locationY><defaultConnector><targetReference>CreateDraft</targetReference></defaultConnector><defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel><rules><name>HasSavedApplication</name><conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic><conditions><leftValueReference>varT_SavedFormId</leftValueReference><operator>IsNull</operator><rightValue><booleanValue>false</booleanValue></rightValue></conditions><connector><targetReference>SavedApplication</targetReference></connector><label>Yes</label></rules></decisions><description>Portal flow (Screen Flow: Case Address Change Request). A licensee asks to change their mailing address: they enter the new address, upload proof (a Proof of Address checklist item) and certify. The proof waits on a draft until they certify; then the form creates a Case (Origin Web, Type Address Change) in the General Inquiries queue with the new address in its Requested fields, moves the proof to it and deletes the draft. Like the other forms, the draft holds the saved-form link (Save for later shows on My Applications), a saved request is offered to continue, abandoned drafts are discarded (at most three per start), and the last screen links back to My Applications instead of a Finish button that would restart the form. Staff apply it with Apply Address Change. Person accounts only: salons, schools, facilities and manager licenses go through staff. Runs in system context like the other portal forms.</description><environments>Default</environments><formulas><name>forT_EarlierGuid</name><description>The earlier draft's interview GUID, from its saved-form link.</description><dataType>String</dataType><expression>SUBSTITUTE({!LoopThroughEarlierDrafts.SavedApplicationUrl}, "/LPI/s/continue-application?guid=", "")</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forB_AbandonedDraft</name><description>A draft over a day old that was never saved for later was abandoned.</description><dataType>Boolean</dataType><expression>{!LoopThroughEarlierDrafts.CreatedDate} &lt; NOW() - 1</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forT_SavedFormId</name><description>The most recent saved address change (drafts are read newest first).</description><dataType>String</dataType><expression>BLANKVALUE({!varT_SavedFormId}, {!GetEarlierSavedForm.Id})</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forT_SavedApplicationUrl</name><description>Records this form's interview GUID on the draft, as every form does, so a saved form shows on My Applications.</description><dataType>String</dataType><expression>"/LPI/s/continue-application?guid=" &amp; {!$Flow.InterviewGuid}</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forDT_CertifiedLouisiana</name><description>When the applicant certified, moved from GMT to Louisiana (Central) time, daylight saving included. Only for display.</description><dataType>DateTime</dataType><expression>{!varDT_CertifiedDateTime} - IF(AND({!varDT_CertifiedDateTime} &gt;= DATETIMEVALUE(TEXT((DATE(YEAR(DATEVALUE({!varDT_CertifiedDateTime})), 3, 8) + MOD(8 - WEEKDAY(DATE(YEAR(DATEVALUE({!varDT_CertifiedDateTime})), 3, 8)), 7))) &amp; " 08:00:00"), {!varDT_CertifiedDateTime} &lt; DATETIMEVALUE(TEXT((DATE(YEAR(DATEVALUE({!varDT_CertifiedDateTime})), 11, 1) + MOD(8 - WEEKDAY(DATE(YEAR(DATEVALUE({!varDT_CertifiedDateTime})), 11, 1)), 7))) &amp; " 07:00:00")), 5, 6) / 24</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forT_CertifiedLouisianaTime</name><description>When the applicant certified, in Louisiana time, for example November 19, 2026 at 9:54 PM.</description><dataType>String</dataType><expression>CASE(VALUE(MID(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 6, 2)), 1, "January", 2, "February", 3, "March", 4, "April", 5, "May", 6, "June", 7, "July", 8, "August", 9, "September", 10, "October", 11, "November", 12, "December", "") &amp; " " &amp; TEXT(VALUE(MID(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 9, 2))) &amp; ", " &amp; LEFT(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 4) &amp; " at " &amp; TEXT(MOD(VALUE(MID(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 12, 2)) + 11, 12) + 1) &amp; ":" &amp; MID(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 15, 2) &amp; " " &amp; IF(VALUE(MID(TEXT({!forDT_CertifiedLouisiana}), 12, 2)) &lt; 12, "AM", "PM")</expression></formulas><formulas><name>forT_Description</name><description>The Case description: the old and new address and the certification, so staff see the request at a glance.</description><dataT